Study metadata

Study titles, descriptions and accessions are derived from the European
Nucleotide Archive and MGnify, operated by EMBL-EBI. EMBL-EBI places no
restrictions on redistribution beyond those of the original data owners and
asks for attribution as good scientific practice.

  https://www.ebi.ac.uk/about/terms-of-use/

Bibliographic metadata (titles, DOIs, publishers, licence URLs) comes from
Crossref, which places its metadata in the public domain.

Study abstracts taken from publications are reproduced only where the work
carries a Creative Commons licence, and are shown with the publisher, the
licence and the DOI. Abstracts are the one part of Crossref's metadata that
Crossref does not place in the public domain -- they remain subject to
publisher or author copyright -- so abstracts under all-rights-reserved,
text-and-data-mining-only or unstated terms are neither displayed nor stored,
and are absent from the database snapshots distributed from the downloads page
(see new-schema/migrations/0083_drop_non_redistributable_abstracts.sql).
